From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 06:59:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(chat): drop the identity rows and session agent avatars

Single-user single-agent chat repeated the same identity everywhere: every
session row carried a profile avatar plus its name, and every message bubble
printed an author row (profile/alias for user turns, runtime name for assistant
turns). Strip them from the chat surfaces and replace the lost streaming cue.

- SessionListItem: remove the profile row and the showProfile prop; the agent
  logo becomes opt-in via showAgentAvatar (Person still needs it for identity).
- SessionListItem: mark working sessions with a live dot in the title row, so
  the indicator no longer depends on the avatar row being rendered.
- MessageItem/MessageList/HistoryMessageList: add hideAuthor, set by ChatPanel
  and HistoryView; Person keeps its author rows as character identity.
- i18n: add chat.sessionLive for all supported locales.
- tests/harness: assert the live dot and the hidden author rows, and re-home
  the ui-theme baseline keys whose selectors were deleted.
